---
// Homepage capability sections. One section per headline in the approved order.
import LandingIcon from './LandingIcon.astro'
import { SITE_PRODUCT } from '../lib/site'

const panels = [
  {
    name: 'Files',
    text: 'Browse the workspace tree, open diffs, and stage exactly the lines you mean.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Browser',
    text: 'Watch the running app in a live preview while the agent works beside it.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Terminal',
    text: 'Run commands in the workspace with output streamed into the transcript.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Changes',
    text: 'Every edit is tracked per file and per line, held for your review.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Pull Request',
    text: 'Draft the pull request description from the work the agent already did.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Plan',
    text: 'The plan panel shows what the agent intends before a single line moves.'
  }
]

const modes = [
  {
    name: 'Ask',
    text: 'Read-only by design: answers come from your repository without touching it.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Plan',
    text: 'Holds file edits until you approve the plan. Nothing ships without your review.'
  },
  {
    name: 'Agent',
    text: 'Full workspace writes, each one guarded by an approval you give first.'
  }
]
---

<section id="capabilities" class="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="features-title" class="section-title">Six panels, one task, zero app-switching.</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">Every workspace opens in one window, so work flows across panels.</p>
    <div class="card-grid panels-grid">
      {
        panels.map((panel) => (
          <article class="spec-card">
            <h3 class="spec-name mono">{panel.name}</h3>
            <p>{panel.text}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features alt" aria-labelledby="modes-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="modes-title" class="section-title">You decide how much the agent may do.</h2>
    <div class="card-grid modes-grid">
      {
        modes.map((mode) => (
          <article class="spec-card">
            <h3 class="spec-name mono">{mode.name}</h3>
            <p>{mode.text}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="section-note">
      File edits stay subject to approvals: Plan mode holds edits until you approve the plan,
      and Agent mode asks before each write.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features" aria-labelledby="checkpoints-title">
  <div class="wrap checkpoints">
    <h2 id="checkpoints-title" class="section-title">Long work stays resumable.</h2>
    <p>
      Checkpoints snapshot the workspace between steps so a long session returns where it left
      off. They are not Git commits: a checkpoint cannot reverse what your build tools already
      ran, and checkpoints keep the state needed to return to any step. A token estimate line shows the
      expected cost before you run a plan.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features alt" aria-labelledby="models-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="models-title" class="section-title">Bring your own model.</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="spec-card">
        <h3 class="spec-name mono">Initial selection</h3>
        <p>Fresh settings start on local Ollama with <code>qwen2.5</code>, wired and ready.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="spec-card">
        <h3 class="spec-name mono">Cloud providers</h3>
        <p>Nine wired clouds sit beside the local host; pick among nine cloud providers, each enabled by its key.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="spec-card">
        <h3 class="spec-name mono">Any host</h3>
        <p>Point at a custom OpenAI-compatible host when the built-ins do not fit.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="section-note">
      API keys stay in operating-system secure storage; the agent never reads them as text.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features" aria-labelledby="extend-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="extend-title" class="section-title">Extend on purpose, not by default.</h2>
    <p>
      Attach external tool servers as marketplace packages. Nothing attaches on its own: the
      agent only calls servers you attached on purpose.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features alt" aria-labelledby="network-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="network-title" class="section-title">Local by default. Explicit about the network.</h2>
    <p>
      Voice dictation runs Whisper models locally in a utility process. Network calls are opt-in
      and pass through an optional domain allowlist. Version checks never install on their own,
      and rotating logs keep disk use flat.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features" aria-labelledby="memory-docs-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="memory-docs-title" class="section-title">Docs for every step.</h2>
    <p>
      Project memory lives in <code>.vyotiq/memory/</code> inside your repository — separate from memory the agent holds per session. Checkpoints, plans, and approvals are explained
      in the guides.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link mono" href="/docs/start/quickstart">
      Start the quickstart
      <LandingIcon name="arrow-right" size={12} />
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .features {
    padding: 4.5rem 0;
  }

  .features.alt {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .section-lead {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .spec-card {
    background: var(--well);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem;
  }

  .spec-name {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }

  .spec-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .section-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .features > .wrap > p {
    color: var(--fg);
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }
</style>
